      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p>The Logic follows here is:</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cross multiplication of outer numbers gives the middle number.</strong></p>\n\n<p><strong>In Figure 1:</strong></p>\n\n<p>3 × 1 = 3 (Last Number) ; 1 × 5 = 5 (First Number) ;2 × 4 = 8 (Middle Number)</p>\n\n<p><strong>So, the number is 583.</strong></p>\n\n<p><strong>In Figure 2:</strong></p>\n\n<p>5 × 1 = 5 (Last Number) ; 4 × 2 = 8 (First Number); 0 × 9 = 0 (Middle Number)</p>\n\n<p><strong>So, the number is 805.</strong></p>\n\n<p>Similarly;</p>\n\n<p><strong>In Figure 3:</strong></p>\n\n<p>8 × 0 = 0 (Last Number); 1 × 7 = 7 (First Number) ;2 × 3 = 6 (Middle Number)</p>\n\n<p><strong>So, the number is 760.</strong></p>\n",
